cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "tcs-xtce: an XTCE compiler, editor and packet runtime"
abstract: >-
  tcs-xtce compiles a mission's XTCE (XML Telemetric and Command
  Exchange) definitions of commands and telemetry into typed data
  structures with bit-packed binary encoders and decoders, in C/C++, Rust
  and Python, which agree with one another byte for byte. Programs check
  that they were built from the same definition by comparing digests that
  every language computes the same way, instead of carrying field names
  or tags in each packet. It includes an XTCE editor and tcsxtce, the
  runtime the generated code runs on aboard and in the operations center.
authors:
  - name: "TCSpecial Team"
version: 0.7.1
date-released: 2026-11-15
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/vomlehn/tcs-xtce"
keywords:
  - XTCE
  - telemetry
  - telecommand
  - code generation
  - packet encoding
  - spacecraft
  - Rust
